// src/v4/std/diagnostic.dag
//
// Scope: fail-closed Diagnostic schema with structural reason+at+correction.
//        Per STRUCTURE.md architectural commitment #3, the schema CARRIES
//        the suggested-correction obligation — the substrate must be able
//        to enforce THESIS:103-105 "show the correct code", so the field
//        is part of the type, not optional bolt-on.
// Anchor: THESIS.md "Show the correct code" §103-105 + INVARIANTS P3
//
// Owns:
//   - Diagnostic { reason: NamedReason, at: Locus, correction: Correction }
//   - NamedReason enum (structural; never opaque string)
//   - Locus = port|node|file|span
//   - Correction = Suggested(Node) | Unavailable(NoCorrectionReason)
//     (typed sum — NOT Option<Node>. "no correction available" is
//     a structural Unavailable case carrying a NoCorrectionReason, never a
//     bare None enforced by convention. Type-enforced per INVARIANTS P2,
//     not API-enforced.)
//     The suggested correction is a Node — the bounded kernel says Node is
//     the ONLY recursive type, so a subtree of Nodes IS a Node (no separate
//     "NodeFragment": that would be a decorative alias the compiler sees
//     through, per feedback_nodes_are_nodes + feedback_naming_is_aliasing).
//     WHERE the correction applies is not carried by the fragment — it is
//     the Diagnostic's own `at: Locus`.
//   - NoCorrectionReason = UserInputBoundary | AmbiguousIntent
//     | ExternalContractUnknown   (closed — the exhaustive partition of
//     "why can't the fix be mechanically derived": intent the compiler
//     cannot know (one missing user choice = UserInputBoundary; many valid
//     candidates = AmbiguousIntent) OR information the compiler cannot see
//     (behind an external contract = ExternalContractUnknown). NO "..." —
//     a 4th reason at fill-time is a substrate-extension STOP, not a
//     silent escape. Every "no fix" thus answers WHY structurally.)
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/node.dag: Conj, Disj
//   (String for messages is the kernel-ambient String — no import)
//
// Status: T-3 modeled 2026-05-15 (smart-eagle-570). The I/O contract in
// this header is immutable for downstream workers. Splitting this file
// requires explicit operator ratification (substrate extension = stop
// signal).


module v4.std.diagnostic


import v4.std.node { Node }


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Modeling notes (read before validating against the anchor)
//
// SCHEMA FILE. diagnostic.dag declares the fail-closed `Diagnostic`
// type and its three structural carriers — it owns no producer logic.
// The pipeline stages (T-6 tokenize … T-22 eval) and the lens reads
// CONSTRUCT `Diagnostic` values; this file is the shape they construct
// to (INVARIANTS P3 — every failure path is a typed Diagnostic, never a
// panic, never a silent `None`).
//
// NO MESSAGE STRING. A `Diagnostic` carries `reason: NamedReason`, not a
// free-text `message: String`. The reason is a STRUCTURAL code; its
// human-readable rendering lives in a boundary table consulted only at
// diagnostic-render time — exactly the std/node.dag K-1 discipline that
// keeps an opaque `Symbol`'s spelling out of kernel/lens logic. A
// `String` message would be the opaque-string heuristic-smuggling
// channel K-1 forecloses (feedback_opaque_strings_attract_heuristics),
// and is the brief's explicit STOP ("string-typed reason").
//
// NAMEDREASON IS THE std/node.dag-`Connective` PATTERN (operator-
// ratified 2026-05-15). It is a CLOSED central enum: a new reason is an
// edit to THIS declaration — a visible diff routed to operator
// ratification (STRUCTURE.md A3) — never an open `Other` variant and
// never a `String` escape. It is SEEDED here with only the reasons the
// substrate built so far (std/node.dag) can justify; the pipeline-stage
// and extdeps tasks add their own reasons by that same ratified-diff
// mechanism (e.g. T-4.5 file_system.dag read-failure modes) as they
// land — the growth mechanism of `Connective`/`Behavior`.
//
// Every coproduct below carries the full Practice-4 🟢/🟡/🔴
// classification + 4-pattern ledger (modeling-discipline.md §4 —
// operator-ratified binding 2026-05-15). The `Diagnostic` record is a
// Conj, not a coproduct, so no ledger applies to it.


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// NamedReason — the closed, structural classifier of WHY a Diagnostic
// fired. Never an opaque `String` (header + brief STOP). WHERE the fault
// is lives in the Diagnostic's own `at: Locus`; WHAT to do about it in
// `correction: Correction` — so a reason variant is a bare structural
// tag carrying no payload.
//
// Seeded (per the node.dag-`Connective` pattern, modeling notes above)
// with exactly the node-well-formedness faults std/node.dag's
// `node_well_formed` whole-tree check distinguishes:
//   - EdgeLabelKindMismatch — an `Edge`'s label KIND is wrong for its
//     parent connective's discipline: a `Named` edge under a positional
//     connective (Arrow/Cardinality/Instantiation), a `Positional` edge
//     under a labeled connective (Conj/Disj), or any edge under `Atom`.
//     This is the single illegal state std/node.dag's edge-discipline
//     invariant (its `EdgeDiscipline` block) names "label-KIND
//     mismatch" — the violation `edges_conform` rejects.
//   - DuplicateEdgeName — a labeled connective (Conj/Disj) has two
//     children sharing one `Named` key. A `Named` edge is an ADDRESS; a
//     duplicate key makes "address a child by name" ambiguous. This is
//     the violation std/node.dag's `all_names_distinct` rejects.
//
// CLOSED. A third reason is an edit to THIS declaration — a visible diff
// routed to operator ratification (STRUCTURE.md A3); there is no `Other`.
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / INVARIANTS P1 / modeling-
// discipline.md §4) — classification: 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger —
// four patterns attempted:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: a reason is consumed UNIFORMLY — every
//      Diagnostic renderer and every diagnostic-exhaustiveness TestClaim
//      branches over the whole reason set; it is not a per-consumer fact
//      to scatter to distinct DAG locations.
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: the only "data" form is a `reason:
//      String`, which is precisely the opaque-string heuristic-
//      smuggling channel K-1 forecloses and the brief's explicit STOP.
//      A closed structural enum is the faithful form (M4 — a closed set
//      is an enum, not a stringly proxy).
//   3. Algebraic form — N/A: a diagnostic reason is not an algebra
//      carrier; the variants are the structural-failure codomain of
//      std/node.dag's `node_well_formed`, which is their richest source
//      — pointing elsewhere would be circular.
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: a Diagnostic fires for EXACTLY ONE reason;
//      the variants are mutually-exclusive alternatives, never
//      simultaneous coordinates of one value.
// Terminal: an irreducible closed classifier of structural-failure
// kinds — the std/node.dag-`Connective` pattern (closed; growth = a
// ratified diff to this declaration).
type NamedReason
  = EdgeLabelKindMismatch
  | DuplicateEdgeName


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Locus — WHERE a Diagnostic points. A Diagnostic carries exactly one
// `Locus` (`at`); the four variants are GRANULARITY alternatives — the
// fault is located at one of a pipeline port, a substrate `Node`, a
// source file, or a source span.
//
// node-only (brief): every payload is built from std/node.dag substrate
// types or the kernel-ambient `Int` —
//   - PortLocus / FileLocus carry an opaque `Symbol` identity (K-1 — a
//     port name / file path is an identifier, never a readable `String`
//     the kernel can branch on).
//   - NodeLocus carries the offending `Node` itself.
//   - SpanLocus carries a half-open `[start, end)` offset pair over the
//     kernel-ambient `Int` — the minimal source-range representation,
//     needing no source-text substrate (none exists at T-3).
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / INVARIANTS P1 / modeling-
// discipline.md §4) — classification: 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger —
// four patterns attempted:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: the locus is consumed uniformly by the
//      diagnostic renderer; it is not a per-consumer fact.
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: the four variants carry DIFFERENT
//      payload shapes (a `Symbol`; a `Node`; an `Int` pair). Collapsing
//      to a flat `{ kind, symbol?, node?, start?, end? }` record makes
//      illegal combinations representable (a `NodeLocus` carrying a
//      span) — the inverse of P2 (illegal states unrepresentable).
//   3. Algebraic form — N/A: a source locus is not an algebra carrier;
//      there is no richer std/ structure it traces to.
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: a Diagnostic points at EXACTLY ONE locus
//      granularity — the variants are alternatives, not simultaneous
//      coordinates (a fault is reported at the port OR node OR file OR
//      span, the most specific the producer knows).
// Terminal: an irreducible set of source-location granularities at the
// diagnostic boundary.
type Locus
  = PortLocus { port: Symbol }
  | NodeLocus { node: Node }
  | FileLocus { file: Symbol }
  | SpanLocus { start: Int, end: Int }


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// NoCorrectionReason — the exhaustive partition of WHY a fix cannot be
// mechanically derived. Carried by `Correction.Unavailable` so that "no
// fix" is itself a structural answer, never a bare absence.
//
// Two root causes, three cells (header):
//   - intent the compiler cannot KNOW:
//       UserInputBoundary — one missing user choice; the fix is a
//         single decision only the author can make.
//       AmbiguousIntent — many valid candidate fixes; the compiler
//         will not pick one (picking = fabrication, the no-engine STOP).
//   - information the compiler cannot SEE:
//       ExternalContractUnknown — the fix lies behind an external
//         contract (an extdeps boundary) the compiler cannot inspect.
//
// CLOSED — no "…". A fourth "why no fix" is a substrate-extension STOP
// (header), an edit to this declaration routed to operator ratification.
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / INVARIANTS P1 / modeling-
// discipline.md §4) — classification: 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger —
// four patterns attempted:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: consumed uniformly by the renderer that
//      explains why no fix is offered; not a per-consumer fact.
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: the only "data" form is a `String`
//      reason — the opaque-string STOP again; the closed three-way
//      partition is the faithful form.
//   3. Algebraic form — N/A: not an algebra carrier; the variants are
//      the partition of an epistemic boundary, with no richer std/
//      source.
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: a "no fix" answers EXACTLY ONE why — the
//      two root causes (can't-know / can't-see) are disjoint and the
//      three cells mutually exclusive; never simultaneous coordinates.
// Terminal: the exhaustive, irreducible partition of "why can't the fix
// be mechanically derived" — every no-fix case answers structurally.
type NoCorrectionReason
  = UserInputBoundary
  | AmbiguousIntent
  | ExternalContractUnknown


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Correction — the structural answer to "show the correct code"
// (THESIS §103-105, STRUCTURE.md architectural commitment #3). Every
// Diagnostic carries one; the schema makes the fix obligation type-
// enforced, not a convention.
//
//   - Suggested carries the fix as a `Node` — the bounded kernel's one
//     recursive type, so a subtree of Nodes IS a Node; there is no
//     separate `NodeFragment` alias (the header's nodes-are-nodes
//     point). WHERE the fix applies is NOT carried here — it is the
//     Diagnostic's own `at: Locus`.
//   - Unavailable carries a `NoCorrectionReason`. "No fix" is a
//     structural case that answers WHY, never a bare `None` — this is
//     the brief's explicit STOP ("Option<Node>") and INVARIANTS P2
//     (type-enforced, not API-enforced).
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / INVARIANTS P1 / modeling-
// discipline.md §4) — classification: 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger —
// four patterns attempted:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: every Diagnostic consumer that surfaces
//      the fix handles BOTH arms (render the suggested `Node`, or render
//      the no-fix reason); it is not a per-consumer fact.
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: the arms carry DIFFERENT shapes (a
//      `Node`; a `NoCorrectionReason`). Collapsing to `{ has_fix: Bool,
//      node?, reason? }` ratifies exactly the bare-`None` illegal state
//      the header forbids — `has_fix: true` with no `node` becomes
//      representable (the inverse of P2).
//   3. Algebraic form — N/A: a correction is not an algebra carrier;
//      there is no richer std/ structure it traces to.
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: a Diagnostic either HAS a mechanically-
//      derivable fix OR does not — disjoint alternatives, never
//      simultaneous coordinates.
// Terminal: the irreducible two-case answer to the "show the correct
// code" obligation — a typed sum, never `Option<Node>`.
type Correction
  = Suggested { node: Node }
  | Unavailable { reason: NoCorrectionReason }


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Diagnostic — the fail-closed typed error (INVARIANTS P3). Every
// failure path in the pipeline and every empty lens read surfaces as a
// `Diagnostic` value; there is no panic and no silent `None`.
//
// Three structural fields, no free-text message (modeling notes):
//   reason      — WHY it fired (a structural `NamedReason`, not String)
//   at          — WHERE it points (a `Locus`)
//   correction  — the "show the correct code" answer (a `Correction`)
//
// This is a record (Conj), not a coproduct — no Practice-4 ledger.
type Diagnostic {
  reason: NamedReason
  at: Locus
  correction: Correction
}
